                        "target_lang_word": "Dalai Lama",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Dalai Lama",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "470be1e1-cf79-3a06-b9b6-88bd23a4d8a2",
                                        "entry_id": "df5f59e5-5650-31bf-8b1e-32a66e6dae89",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "höchster Lama innerhalb der Hierarchie der Gelug-Schule des tibetischen Buddhismus; Geistiger Führer der Tibeter"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d43504d-0bb9-4e6a-8467-096fdb78cdef",
                                                "sense_id": "470be1e1-cf79-3a06-b9b6-88bd23a4d8a2",
                                                "text": "Der […] Dalai Lama gilt als Symbol des gewaltlosen Widerstands der Tibeter gegen die chinesische Besatzung ihrer Heimat."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a508f980-db96-44a2-9858-cb3118adc30e",
                        "source_entry_id": "57d89dba-041e-315b-8789-ee0d435f72c1",
                        "source_sense_id": "323a1f10-57a3-3ed7-8aec-8625c91978d7",
                        "source_sense_description": "chef religieux bouddhiste",
                        "target_lang_word": "Dalai Lama",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Dalai Lama",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e22b1e3a-bdcd-3ede-ab4f-d8d38df547cf",
                                        "entry_id": "f9faaec4-db62-3f8f-8e3d-55486089db35",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The supreme head of Tibetan Buddhism, believed to be an incarnation of Avalokitesvara, and considered the spiritual leader of the Tibetan people."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Tibetan"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1be78b31-1abc-4983-b7c9-c38fe8674135",
                                                "sense_id": "e22b1e3a-bdcd-3ede-ab4f-d8d38df547cf",
                                                "text": "Of the Mongall Tartars.\nThe Mongalls are a numerous people, and occupy a large extent of country, from this place to the Kallgan, which ſignifies the everlaſting Wall, or the great wall of China. From this wall they ſtretch themſelves northward as far as the river Amoor; and from the Amoor, weſtward, to the Baykail ſea ; where they border with the territories of the Kontayſha, or prince of the black Kalmucks. On the ſouth, they are bounded by a nation called Tonguts, among whom the Delay Lama has his residence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61d3223f-39f1-40a0-bc48-79603dbf57c0",
                                                "sense_id": "e22b1e3a-bdcd-3ede-ab4f-d8d38df547cf",
                                                "text": "Szechuen troops defending recognized Chinese territory against the raids of the Tibetans declare that by crossing the Kinsha River the forces of the Da Lai Lama have violated the recent truce. The truce established the stream as the boundary between Tibet and China Proper."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9891638e-430f-478f-b8c0-520de085ef9c",
                                                "sense_id": "e22b1e3a-bdcd-3ede-ab4f-d8d38df547cf",
                                                "text": "I got a laugh from the Chinese audience when I said I thought that if Jiang and the Dalai Lama did meet, they would like each other very much."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "478dd19d-a3da-4e2b-88dc-4e08b421ff5f",
                                                "sense_id": "e22b1e3a-bdcd-3ede-ab4f-d8d38df547cf",
                                                "text": "I was pleased that President George W. Bush presented the Congressional Gold Medal to the Dalai Lama at the Capitol in October 2007.\nIn March 2008, I led a Congressional delegation to India. Part of our mission was to meet with the Dalai Lama in Dharamsala, the headquarters of Tibetan exiles."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8fd9c01-36ab-4c1b-a1bc-d251d4e328b9",
                                                "sense_id": "e22b1e3a-bdcd-3ede-ab4f-d8d38df547cf",
                                                "text": "At the 2007 APEC Summit in Sydney, I told President Hu I planned to attend a ceremony where the Dalai Lama would receive the Congressional Gold Medal. The Buddhist leader was a source of distress for the Chinese government, which accused him of stirring up separatists in Tibet. I met with the Dalai Lama five times during my presidency, and I found him to be a charming, peaceful man. I told China’s leaders they should not fear him. “This is not meant as a slap at China,” I said, “but as a measure of my respect for the Dalai Lama and for the U.S. Congress. You know my strong belief in religious freedom.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
